:Class WebSocketClient

    (⎕ML ⎕IO)←1

    ∇ r←Version
      :Access public shared
      r←'WebSocketClient' '0.9.0' '2026-08-24'
    ∇

    ∇ r←Documentation
    ⍝ return link to documentation
      :Access public shared
      r←'See https://dyalog.github.io/WebSocketClient/'
    ∇

    ⍝ Connect-related fields
    :field public URL←''                           ⍝ WebSocket server URL
    :field public Params←''                        ⍝ request parameters
    :field public Headers←0 2⍴⊂''                  ⍝ request headers - name, value
    :field public Auth←''                          ⍝ Credentials: one of '' 'token' ('userid' 'password')
    :field public AuthType←''                      ⍝ typical values are '', 'BASIC', 'BEARER', 'TOKEN'
    :field public Origin←'null'                    ⍝ Origin header value
    :field public HeaderSubstitution←''            ⍝ for injecting environment variables into headers
    :field public Secret←1                         ⍝ hide credentials in Config
    :field public AutoUpgrade←1                    ⍝ automatically accept WebSocket upgrade response
    :field public MaxRedirections←2                ⍝ maximum redirect "hops" that we will follow
    :field public Shared Debug←0                   ⍝ set to 1 to disable trapping, 2 to stop just before creating client

    ⍝ WebSocket Specific headers
    :field public Protocol←''                      ⍝ Sec-WebSocket-Protocol header value(s)
    :field public Extensions←''                    ⍝ Sec-WebSocket-Extensions header value(s)
    :field public WSUpgradeResponse←''             ⍝ namespace containing the server response to the upgrade request

    ⍝ WebSocket Event Hooks
    :field public OnWSUpgrade←''                   ⍝ automatic upgrade response
    :field public OnWSResponse←''                  ⍝ validation of upgrade response
    :field public OnWSReceive←''                   ⍝ message reception
    :field public OnClose←''                       ⍝ WebSocket close event
    :field public OnError←''                       ⍝ WSError event handler

    ⍝ Proxy-related fields - only used if connecting through a proxy server
    :field public ProxyURL←''                      ⍝ address of the proxy server
    :field public ProxyAuth←''                     ⍝ authentication string, if any, for the proxy server
    :field public ProxyAuthType←''                 ⍝ authentication type, if any, for the proxy server
    :field public ProxyHeaders←0 2⍴⊂''             ⍝ any headers that the proxy server might need
    :field public ProxyResponse←''                 ⍝ namespace containing the response from proxy server
    :field public HttpHeaders←''                   ⍝ headers sent back by server on proxy CONNECT

    ⍝ Conga-related fields
    :field public BufferSize←200000                ⍝ Conga buffersize
    :field public WaitTime←5000                    ⍝ Timeout in ms on Conga Wait call
    :field public Cert←⍬                           ⍝ X509 instance if using HTTPS (wss)
    :field public SSLFlags←32                      ⍝ SSL/TLS flags - 32 = accept cert without checking it
    :field public Priority←'NORMAL:!CTYPE-OPENPGP' ⍝ GnuTLS priority string
    :field public PublicCertFile←''                ⍝ if not using an X509 instance, this is the client public certificate file
    :field public PrivateKeyFile←''                ⍝ if not using an X509 instance, this is the client private key file
    :field public shared LDRC                      ⍝ WebSocketClient-set reference to Conga after CongaRef has been resolved
    :field public shared CongaPath←''              ⍝ path to user-supplied conga workspace (assumes shared libraries are in the same path)
    :field public shared CongaRef←''               ⍝ user-supplied reference to Conga library
    :field public shared CongaVersion←''           ⍝ set when Conga is initialized

    ⍝ Operational fields
    :field public readonly shared ValidFormUrlEncodedChars←'&=ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-._~*+~%'

    ⍝ Status fields
    :field public rc←¯1
    :field public msg←''
    :field public Connection←''
    :field public LastWaitResponse←''
    :field public Connected←0
    :field public Data←''          ⍝ contains data element of LDRC.Wait result if Conga could not parse it as HTTP
    :field public ErrorInfo←''     ⍝ capture ⎕DMX from errors in Listen
    :field public HttpStatus←⍬
    :field public HttpMessage←''
    :field public HttpVersion←''
    :field public Redirections←⍬
    :field public Secure←⍬
    :field public Host←''
    :field public Port←⍬
    :field public Path←''
    :field public PeerCert←''
    :field public MsgState         ⍝ namespace containing the current message state

    :field _fragmentType←0         ⍝ datatype (1 or 2) for fragmented messages
    :field _done←0                 ⍝ flag to indicate to stop Listen
    :field _listenerThread←⍬       ⍝ thread that Listener is running on

    :property ListenerThread
    :access public
        ∇ r←Get
          r←_listenerThread
        ∇
    :endproperty

    ∇ (rc msg)←onWSUpgrade waitData
    ⍝ waitData is the data element of WebSocket server's response
    ⍝ parseWSUpgrade parses the data element into HTTP Version, Status, Message, Headers and Payload
    ⍝ rc should be 0 if the WebSocket is okay to exist, non-0 otherwise
    ⍝ onWSUpgrade is called when AutoUpgrade=1
      (rc msg)←0 ''
      WSUpgradeResponse←parseWSUpgrade waitData
      :If ~0∊⍴OnWSUpgrade
          (rc msg)←⎕THIS(##⍎OnWSUpgrade)WSUpgradeResponse
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ (rc msg)←onWSResponse waitData
    ⍝ waitData is the data element of WebSocket server's response
    ⍝ parseWSUpgrade parses the data element into HTTP Version, Status, Message, Headers and Payload
    ⍝ rc should be 0 if the WebSocket is okay to exist, non-0 otherwise
    ⍝ onWSUpgrade is called when AutoUpgrade=0
      (rc msg)←0 ''
      WSUpgradeResponse←parseWSUpgrade waitData
      :If ~0∊⍴OnWSResponse
          (rc msg)←⎕THIS(##⍎OnWSResponse)WSUpgradeResponse
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ onWSReceive waitData;final;opcode;payload
    ⍝ waitData is the data of the WSReceive event [1] payload [2] final? [3] opcode
      (payload final opcode)←waitData
      :If 0≠opcode ⍝ first (or only) frame
          MsgState.(buffer payload final opcode)←payload payload final opcode
      :Else ⍝ 0=opcode → continuation frame
          MsgState.buffer,←payload
          MsgState.(payload final)←payload final
      :EndIf  

      :If ~0∊⍴OnWSReceive ⍝ user-defined hook function?
          ⎕THIS(##⍎OnWSReceive)MsgState
      :Else ⍝ default behavior
          :If MsgState.final
              ⎕←'>>> ',⍕MsgState.buffer
          :EndIf
      :EndIf
     
      :If MsgState.final ⍝ if final, reset MsgState
          MsgState.(buffer payload final opcode)←'' '' ¯1 ¯1
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ (rc msg)←onClose waitResponse
    ⍝ waitResponse is [1] Conga return code, [2] Conga object name, [3] Conga event, [4] any data
      (rc msg)←0 'WebSocket Closed'
      :If ~0∊⍴OnClose
          (rc msg)←⎕THIS(##⍎OnClose)waitResponse
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ (rc msg)←onError waitResponse
    ⍝ waitResponse is [1] Conga return code, [2] Conga object name, [3] Conga event, [4] any data
      (rc msg)←0('WebSocket Error: ',⍕waitResponse)
      :If ~0∊⍴OnError
          (rc msg)←⎕THIS(##⍎OnError)waitResponse
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ make
    ⍝ No argument constructor
      :Access public
      :Implements constructor
      makeCommon
    ∇

    ∇ make1 args;settings;invalid
    ⍝ Constructor arguments - [URL Protocol OnWSReceive OnWSUpgrade Headers Params]
      :Access public
      :Implements constructor
      :If ~0∊⍴args
          args←(eis⍣({9.1≠⎕NC⊂,'⍵'}⊃args)⊢args)
          :Select {⊃⎕NC⊂,'⍵'}⊃args
          :Case 2.1 ⍝ array
              (URL OnWSReceive OnWSUpgrade Protocol Headers Params)←6↑args,(⍴args)↓URL OnWSReceive OnWSUpgrade Protocol Headers Params
          :Case 9.1 ⍝ namespace
              :If 0∊⍴invalid←(settings←args.⎕NL ¯2.1 ¯9.1)~(⎕NEW⊃⊃⎕CLASS ⎕THIS).⎕NL ¯2.2
                  args{⍎⍵,'←⍺⍎⍵'}¨settings
              :Else ⋄ ('Invalid WebSocketClient setting(s): ',,⍕invalid)⎕SIGNAL 11
              :EndIf
          :Else ⋄ 'Invalid constructor argument'⎕SIGNAL 11
          :EndSelect
      :EndIf
      makeCommon
    ∇

    ∇ makeCommon
      MsgState←(buffer:'' ⋄ payload:'' ⋄ final:¯1 ⋄ opcode:¯1)
      setDisplayFormat ⎕THIS
    ∇

    ∇ update arg
      :Implements Trigger URL, Connected, rc, msg
      setDisplayFormat ⎕THIS
    ∇

    ∇ setDisplayFormat ns;conn;url;connected;r;m
      :Access public
      r←' rc: ',⍕{6::⍬⊣⎕←'rc missing' ⋄ ⍵.rc}ns
      m←' msg: ',⍕{6::''⊣⎕←'msg missing' ⋄ ⍵.msg}ns
      url←{6::''⊣⎕←'URL missing' ⋄ ⍵.URL}ns
      connected←{6::0⊣⎕←'Connected missing' ⋄ ⍵.Connected}ns
      conn←' ',(4×connected)↓'Not Connected ',(1+0∊⍴url)⊃((url∨.≠' ')/'to ',∊⍕url)'(no URL specified)'
      ⎕DF 2⌽' ][',2↓∊' |'∘,¨r m conn
    ∇

    ∇ Goodbye
      :Implements destructor
      {}{0::'' ⋄ LDRC.Names'.'⊣LDRC.Close ⍵}⍣(~0∊⍴Connection)⊢Connection
      ⎕TKILL _listenerThread
    ∇

    ∇ r←Config;i;m
    ⍝ Returns current configuration
      :Access public
      r←↑{6::⍵'not set' ⋄ ⍵(⍎⍵)}¨(⎕THIS⍎'⎕NL ¯2.2 ¯2.3')~⊂'ValidFormUrlEncodedChars'
      :If ∨/m←(≢r)≥i←r[;1]⍳'Auth' 'ProxyAuth'
      :AndIf Secret
          r[m/i;2]←⊂'>>> Secret setting is 1 <<<'
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←Connect
    ⍝ Attempt to connect
      :Access public
      :Trap Debug↓0
          :If ~0∊⍴Connection ⍝ already have a client?
          :AndIf {0::0 ⋄ 'Connected'≡2 3⊃LDRC.Describe ⍵}Connection ⍝ Client connected?
              →0⊣r←(rc msg)←0 'Already connected'
          :Else
              reset ⍝ reset all connection-related status
              r←(rc msg)←connect
          :EndIf
      :Else ⍝ :Trap
          r←(rc msg)←¯1('Unexpected ',⊃{⍺,' at ',⍵}/2↑⎕DMX.DM)
      :EndTrap
    ∇

    ∇ reset
    ⍝ reset settings before connect
      (rc Connected)←¯1 0
      HttpStatus←Redirections←Secure←Port←⍬
      msg←Connection←LastWaitResponse←''
      Data←ErrorInfo←'' ⍝ Conga's unparsed data, ⎕DMX from errors in Listen
      HttpVersion←HttpMessage←HttpHeaders←''
      Host←Path←PeerCert←''
      WSUpgradeResponse←ProxyResponse←''
      MsgState.(buffer payload final opcode)←'' '' ¯1 ¯1
      setDisplayFormat ⎕THIS
    ∇


    ∇ (rc msg)←Send payload;data;fin;type;opcode
    ⍝ payload is [1] character or sint data {2} final?
      :Access public
      (rc msg)←¯1 ''
      :If 0∊⍴Connection
          msg←'No client connection has been established'
      :Else
          (data fin)←2↑(⊆,payload),1
          type←2*~isChar data
     
          ⍝ _fragmentType either
          ⍝  =0 - meaning no previous fragment
          ⍝  ≠0 - meaning it's the datatype of previous fragment(s)
          :If ~_fragmentType∊0,type
              →∆END⊣msg←'Datatype is not the same as previous fragment (',(⍕_fragmentType),')'
          :EndIf
     
          :If fin=1 ⍝ if this is the final (or only) fragment
              opcode←type×_fragmentType=0 ⍝ opcode is type if not a continuation fragment
              _fragmentType←0
          :Else ⍝ fin≠1
              opcode←type×_fragmentType=0
              _fragmentType←type
          :EndIf
     
          :Trap Debug↓0
              :If 0≠rc←⊃LDRC.Send Connection(data fin opcode)
                  msg←'Conga send failure: ',⍕rc
              :EndIf
          :Else
              msg←(⊃⎕DMX.EM),' occurred trying to send'
          :EndTrap
      :EndIf
     ∆END:
    ∇

    ∇ r←Close;ts
      :Access public
      :If 0∊⍴_listenerThread
          →0⊣r←(rc msg)←0 'Not listening'
      :EndIf
     
      :If _done
          →0⊣r←(rc msg)←0 'Already closed'
      :EndIf
     
      _done←1  ⍝ signal to listener to terminate
      ts←⎕AI[3]
      :While (_listenerThread∊⎕TNUMS)∧⎕AI[3]<ts+WaitTime×1.1
      :EndWhile
     
      :If _listenerThread∊⎕TNUMS
          ⎕TKILL _listenerThread
      :EndIf
      Connection←''
      r←(rc msg)←0 'Closed'
    ∇

    ∇ r←New args
    ⍝ Shared method to create new WebSocketClient
    ⍝ args - [URL Headers Protocol Cert SSLFlags Priority]
      :Access public shared
      :Trap Debug↓0
          :If 0∊⍴args
              r←##.⎕NEW ⎕THIS
          :Else
              r←##.⎕NEW ⎕THIS(eis⍣(9.1≠nameClass⊃args)⊢args)
          :EndIf
          r.(rc msg)←0 'Created'
      :Else
          setDisplayFormat r←(rc:-⎕DMX.EN ⋄ msg:⎕DMX.EM ⋄ Connected:0 ⋄ URL:'')
          →∆EXIT
      :EndTrap
     ∆EXIT:
    ∇

    ∇ r←Init
      :Access Public
      :If 0=⊃(rc msg)←Initialize
          msg←'Initialized'
      :EndIf
      r←(rc msg)
    ∇

    ∇ (rc msg)←Initialize;root;n;congaCopied;class;path;ns;nc;ind
      (rc msg)←¯1 ''
      :Hold 'WSClientInit'
          ⍝↓↓↓ Check if LDRC exists (VALUE ERROR (6) if not), and is LDRC initialized? (NONCE ERROR (16) if not)
          :If {6 16 999::1 ⋄ ''≡LDRC:1 ⋄ 0⊣LDRC.Describe'.'}''
              LDRC←''
              :If ~0∊⍴CongaRef  ⍝ did the user supply a reference to Conga?
                  :If 0∊⍴LDRC←ResolveCongaRef CongaRef
                      msg,⍨←'Could not initialize Conga using CongaRef "',(⍕CongaRef),'" due to '
                      →∆END
                  :EndIf
              :Else ⍝ try to find Conga or DRC in ## and #
                  :For root :In ∪## #
                      ns←'Conga' 'DRC'
                      :If ~0∊⍴ind←⍸<\9=nc←⌊root nameClass ns
                          ns←ind⊃ns
                          nc←ind⊃nc
                          :Leave
                      :EndIf
                  :EndFor
     
                  :If 9=nc ⍝ did we find one?
                      :If 0∊⍴LDRC←ResolveCongaRef(root⍎ns)
                          →∆END⊣msg,⍨←'Could not initialize Conga from "',(∊(⍕root)'.'ns),'" due to '
                      :EndIf
                      →∆COPY↓⍨{999::0 ⋄ 1⊣LDRC.Describe'.'}'' ⍝ it's possible that Conga was saved in a semi-initialized state
                  :Else
     ∆COPY: ⍝ couldn't find a valid Conga namespace, try to copy from the conga workspace
                      class←⊃⊃⎕CLASS ⎕THIS
                      :If ~0∊⍴CongaPath
                          CongaPath←∊1 ⎕NPARTS CongaPath,'/'
                          →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴msg←(~⎕NEXISTS CongaPath)/'CongaPath "',CongaPath,'" does not exist'
                          →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴msg←(1≠1 ⎕NINFO CongaPath)/'CongaPath "',CongaPath,'" is not a folder'
                      :EndIf
                      congaCopied←0
                      :For n :In 'Conga' 'DRC'
                          :For path :In (1+0∊⍴CongaPath)⊃(⊂CongaPath)((dyalogRoot,'ws/')'') ⍝ if CongaPath specifiec, use it exclusively
                              :Trap Debug↓0
                                  n class.⎕CY path,'conga'
                                  LDRC←ResolveCongaRef(class⍎n)
                                  :If 0∊⍴LDRC
                                      msg,⍨←n,' was copied from "',path,'conga", but encountered '
                                      →∆END
                                  :EndIf
                                  →∆COPIED⊣congaCopied←1
                              :EndTrap
                          :EndFor
                      :EndFor
                      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴msg←(~congaCopied)/'neither Conga nor DRC were successfully copied'
     ∆COPIED:
                  :EndIf
              :EndIf
          :EndIf
          CongaVersion←LDRC.Version
          LDRC.X509Cert.LDRC←LDRC ⍝ reset X509Cert.LDRC reference
          :If 0≠⊃LDRC.SetProp'.' 'EventMode' 1
              →∆END⊣msg←'Unable to set EventMode on Conga root'
          :EndIf
          :If 0 1≢LDRC.GetProp'.' 'EventMode'
              →∆END⊣msg←'Conga event mode is not enabled'
          :EndIf
          (rc msg)←0 ''
     ∆END:
      :EndHold
    ∇

    ∇ LDRC←ResolveCongaRef CongaRef;failed;z
    ⍝ Attempt to resolve what CongaRef refers to
    ⍝ CongaRef can be a charvec, reference to the Conga or DRC namespaces, or reference to an iConga instance
    ⍝ LDRC is '' if Conga could not be initialized, otherwise it's a reference to the the Conga.LIB instance or the DRC namespace
     
      LDRC←'' ⋄ failed←0
      :Select nameClass CongaRef ⍝ what is it?
      :Case 9.1 ⍝ namespace?  e.g. CongaRef←DRC or Conga
     ∆TRY:
          :Trap Debug↓0
              :If 2 3≢⌊CongaRef.⎕NC'DllVer' 'Init'
                  msg←'it does not refer to a valid Conga interface'
                  →∆EXIT⊣LDRC←''
              :EndIf
              :If ∨/'.Conga'⍷⍕CongaRef ⍝ Conga?
                  LDRC←CongaPath CongaRef.Init'WebSocketClient'
              :ElseIf 0≡⊃CongaRef.Init CongaPath ⍝ DRC?
                  LDRC←CongaRef
              :Else ⍝ should never get to here, but... (paranoia)
                  msg←'it does not refer to a valid Conga interface'
                  →∆EXIT⊣LDRC←''
              :End
          :Else ⍝ if WebSocketClient is reloaded and re-executed in rapid succession, Conga initialization may fail, so we try twice
              :If failed
                  →∆EXIT⊣LDRC←''⊣msg←∊{⍺,(~0∊⍴⍵)/': ',⍵}/⎕DMX.(EM Message)
              :Else
                  →∆TRY⊣failed←1
              :EndIf
          :EndTrap
      :Case 9.2 ⍝ instance?  e.g. CongaRef←Conga.Init ''
          :If 3=⌊|CongaRef.⎕NC⊂'Clt' ⍝ if it looks like a valid Conga reference
              LDRC←CongaRef ⍝ an instance is already initialized
          :EndIf
      :Case 2.1 ⍝ variable?  e.g. CongaRef←'#.Conga'
          :Trap Debug↓0
              :If 9≠z←⎕NC⍕CongaRef
                  →∆EXIT⊣msg←'CongaRef ',(1+z=0)⊃'is invalid' 'was not found'
              :EndIf
              LDRC←ResolveCongaRef(⍎∊⍕CongaRef)
          :Else
              msg←∊{⍺,(~0∊⍴⍵)/': ',⍵}/⎕DMX.(EM Message)
          :EndTrap
      :EndSelect
     ∆EXIT:
    ∇

    ∇ (rc secureParams)←CreateSecureParams certs;cert;flags;priority;public;private;nmt;msg;t
    ⍝ certs is:
    ⍝ cert     - X509Cert instance or (PublicCertFile PrivateKeyFile)
    ⍝ flags    - SSL flags
    ⍝ priority - GnuTLS priority
    ⍝ public   - PublicCertFile
    ⍝ private  - PrivateKeyFile
     
      certs←,⊆certs
      (cert flags priority public private)←5↑certs,(≢certs)↓'' 0 'NORMAL:!CTYPE-OPENPGP' '' ''
     
      LDRC.X509Cert.LDRC←LDRC ⍝ make sure the X509 instance points to the right LDRC
     
      :If 0∊⍴cert ⍝ if X509 (or public private) not supplied
     ∆CHECK:
          ⍝ if cert is empty, check PublicCertFile and PrivateKeyFile
          :If ∨/nmt←(~0∊⍴)¨public private ⍝ either file name not empty?
              :If ∧/nmt ⍝ if so, both need to be non-empty
                  :If ∨/t←{0::1 ⋄ ~⎕NEXISTS ⍵}¨public private ⍝ either file not exist?
                      →∆FAIL⊣msg←'Not found',4↓∊t/'PublicCertFile' 'PrivateKeyFile'{' and ',⍺,' "',(∊⍕⍵),'"'}¨public private
                  :EndIf
                  :Trap Debug↓0
                      cert←⊃LDRC.X509Cert.ReadCertFromFile public
                  :Else
                      →∆FAIL⊣msg←'Unable to decode PublicCertFile "',(∊⍕public),'" as certificate'
                  :EndTrap
                  cert.KeyOrigin←'DER'private
              :Else
                  →∆FAIL⊣msg←(⊃(~nmt)/'PublicCertFile' 'PrivateKeyFile'),' is empty' ⍝ both must be specified
              :EndIf
          :Else
              cert←⎕NEW LDRC.X509Cert
          :EndIf
      :ElseIf 2=⍴cert ⍝ 2-element vector of public/private file names?
          public private←cert
          →∆CHECK
      :ElseIf {0::1 ⋄ 'X509Cert'≢{⊃⊢/'.'(≠⊆⊢)⍵}⍕⎕CLASS ⍵}cert
          →∆FAIL⊣msg←'Invalid certificate parameter'
      :EndIf
      secureParams←('x509'cert)('SSLValidation'flags)('Priority'priority)
      →rc←0
     ∆FAIL:(rc secureParams)←¯1 msg ⍝ failure
    ∇

    ∇ (rc msg)←connect;auth;cert;conx;dat;datalen;defaultPort;err;evt;hdrs;headers;host;obj;onwsreceive;onwsupgrade;options;parms;path;port;protocol;rc;secure;secureParams;simpleChar;timedOut;url;urlparms;z;redirections;t;loc;ret;proxied;proxy
    ⍝ Connect to a WebSocket server
    ⍝ Result: rc  - 0 means we connected, ≠0 otherwise
    ⍝         msg - 'Connected' if we connected, something else hopefully explaining what went wrong if connection failed
     
      (rc msg)←¯1 'no message yet'
     
      URL←,URL
      parms←Params
     
        ⍝ Do some cursory parameter checking
      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴msg←'No URL specified'/⍨0∊⍴URL ⍝ exit early if no URL
      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴msg←'URL is not a simple character vector'/⍨~isSimpleChar URL
      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴msg←'Headers are not character'/⍨(0∊⍴Headers)⍱1↑isChar Headers
     
      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴2⊃(rc msg)←Initialize
     
      redirections←0
     ∆GET:
     
    ⍝ do header initialization here because we may return here on a redirect
      :Trap 7
          hdrs←makeHeaders Headers
      :Else
          →∆END⊣msg←'Improper header format'
      :EndTrap
     
      conx←ConnectionProperties URL
      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴msg←conx.msg
      (protocol secure auth host port path urlparms defaultPort)←conx.(protocol secure auth host port path urlparms defaultPort)
      secure∨←⍲/{0∊⍴⍵}¨Cert PublicCertFile ⍝ we're also secure if we have a cert or a PublicCertFile
     
      :If proxied←~0∊⍴ProxyURL
          :If CongaVersion(~atLeast)3 4 1626 ⍝ Conga build that introduced proxy support
              →∆END⊣msg←'Conga version 3.4.1626 or later is required to use a proxy'
          :EndIf
          proxy←ConnectionProperties ProxyURL
          →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴msg←proxy.msg
          proxy.headers←makeHeaders ProxyHeaders
      :EndIf
     
      (Secure Host Port Path)←secure(lc host)port path
     
      hdrs←'Sec-WebSocket-Extensions'(hdrs addHeader)deb Extensions
      hdrs←'Sec-WebSocket-Protocol'(hdrs addHeader)deb Protocol
     
    ⍝ There are several ways to specify credentials and take priority in the following order
    ⍝ - setting Auth and, optionally, AuthType
    ⍝ - setting the Authorization header directly
    ⍝ - providing credentials in the URL wss://userid:password@foo.com
      :If ~0∊⍴Auth ⍝ is user specified Auth explicitly, use it even if there are credentials in the URL
          :If (1<|≡Auth)∨':'∊Auth ⍝ (userid password) or userid:password
          :AndIf ('basic'≡lc AuthType)∨0∊⍴AuthType
              auth←Base64Encode ¯1↓∊(,⊆Auth),¨':'
              AuthType←'Basic'
          :EndIf
          hdrs←'Authorization'(hdrs setHeader)deb AuthType,' ',⍕auth
      :ElseIf ~0∊⍴auth
          hdrs←'Authorization'(hdrs addHeader)auth
      :EndIf
     
      :If proxied
          :If ~0∊⍴ProxyAuth
              :If (1<|≡ProxyAuth)∨':'∊ProxyAuth ⍝ (userid password) or userid:password
              :AndIf ('basic'≡lc ProxyAuthType)∨0∊⍴ProxyAuthType
                  ProxyAuth←Base64Encode ¯1↓∊(,⊆ProxyAuth),¨':'
                  ProxyAuthType←'Basic'
              :EndIf
              proxy.headers←'Proxy-Authorization'(proxy.headers setHeader)deb ProxyAuthType,' ',⍕ProxyAuth
          :EndIf
          :If ~0∊⍴proxy.auth
              proxy.headers←'Proxy-Authorization'(proxy.headers addHeader)proxy.auth
          :EndIf
      :EndIf
     
      :If ~0∊⍴parms ⍝ do we have any parameters or a content-type
              ⍝ params needs to be URLEncoded and will be appended to the query string
          :If {2≠⎕NC'⍵':0 ⋄ 1≥|≡⍵}parms ⍝ simple vector or scalar and not a reference
              parms←∊⍕parms       ⍝ deal with possible numeric
              parms←UrlEncode⍣(~∧/parms∊ValidFormUrlEncodedChars)⊢parms ⍝ URLEncode if necessary
          :Else ⍝ parms is a namespace or a name/value pairs array
              parms←UrlEncode parms
          :EndIf
          urlparms,←(0∊⍴urlparms)↓'&',parms
          parms←''
      :EndIf
     
      hdrs⌿⍨←~0∊¨≢¨hdrs[;2] ⍝ remove any headers with empty values
     
      secureParams←''
      :If secure
      :AndIf 0≠⊃(rc secureParams)←CreateSecureParams Cert SSLFlags Priority PublicCertFile PrivateKeyFile
          →∆END⊣(rc msg)←rc secureParams
      :EndIf
     
      :If proxied
          proxy.secureParams←''
          :If proxy.secure
          :AndIf 0≠⊃(rc proxy.secureParams)←CreateSecureParams'' 0
              →∆END⊣(rc msg)←rc('PROXY: ',proxy.secureParams)
          :EndIf
      :EndIf
     
      stopIf Debug=2
     
      options←⊂'Options'(LDRC.Options.DecodeHttp+LDRC.Options.WSAutoUpgrade×AutoUpgrade>proxied)
     
    ⍝ Create the client
      :If ~proxied
          :If 0≠⊃(err Connection)←2↑rc←LDRC.Clt''host port'http'BufferSize,secureParams,options
              Connection←''
              →∆END⊣(rc msg)←err('Conga failed to connect to "',host,'": ',,⍕1↓rc)
          :EndIf
      :Else ⍝ proxied
      ⍝ connect to proxy
          :If 0≠⊃(err Connection)←2↑rc←LDRC.Clt''proxy.host proxy.port'http'BufferSize proxy.secureParams,options
              Connection←''
              →∆END⊣(rc msg)←err('Conga proxy client creation failed ',,⍕1↓rc)
          :EndIf
     
      ⍝ connect to proxied host
          :If 0≠err←⊃rc←LDRC.Send Connection('CONNECT'(host,':',⍕port)'HTTP/1.1'(environment proxy.headers)'')
              →∆END⊣(rc msg)←err('Proxy CONNECT failed: ',⍕1↓rc)
          :EndIf
     
          :If 0≠err←⊃rc←LDRC.Wait Connection 1000
              →∆END⊣(rc msg)←err('Proxy CONNECT wait failed: ',∊⍕1↓rc)
          :Else
              (err obj evt dat)←4↑rc
     
              :If evt≢'HTTPHeader'
                  →∆END⊣(rc msg)←¯1('Proxy CONNECT did not respond with HTTPHeader event: ',∊⍕1↓rc)
              :EndIf
     
              ProxyResponse←⎕NS''
              ProxyResponse.(version status message headers payload)←dat,⊂''
              :If 0<⊃toInt{0∊⍴⍵:'0' ⋄ ⍵}ProxyResponse.headers GetHeader'Content-Length' ⍝ is there any content?
                  ProxyResponse.payload←⊂LDRC.Wait Connection 1000 ⍝ capture what should be an HTTPBody response
              :EndIf
     
              :If '200'≢ProxyResponse.status
                  →∆END⊣(rc msg)←¯1 'Proxy CONNECT response failed, ProxyResponse has the response from the proxy server'
              :EndIf
          :EndIf
     
      ⍝ if secure, upgrade to SSL
          :If secure
              cert←1 2⊃secureParams
          :AndIf 0≠⊃err←LDRC.SetProp Connection'StartTLS'(cert.AsArg,('SSLValidation' 0)('Address'host))
              →∆END⊣(rc msg)←err('Proxy failed to upgrade to secure connection: ',∊⍕err)
          :EndIf
     
          :If AutoUpgrade
          :AndIf 0≠⊃err←LDRC.SetProp Connection'Options'LDRC.Options.(DecodeHttp+WSAutoUpgrade)
              →∆END⊣(rc msg)←err('Could not set WSAutoUpgrade on proxied connection: ',∊⍕err)
          :EndIf
      :EndIf  ⍝ end of proxy stuff
     
      ⍝ Request the WebSocket upgrade
      :If 0≠⊃err←LDRC.SetProp Connection'WSUpgrade'((path,(0∊⍴urlparms)↓'?',urlparms)host(formatHeaders environment hdrs))
          →∆END⊣(rc msg)←(⊃err)('Conga "WSUpgrade" failed: ',⍕2↓err)
      :EndIf
     
      :If 0≠err←1⊃ret←LDRC.Wait Connection WaitTime
          msg←'Conga wait error ',,⍕err ⍝ some other error (very unlikely)
      :EndIf
     
      (err obj evt dat)←4↑ret
      :Select evt
      :Case 'HTTPHeader' ⍝ should only get this on a redirection
          :If 1=≡dat
              →∆END⊣(rc Data msg)←¯1 dat'Conga failed to parse the response HTTP header' ⍝ HTTP header parsing failed?
          :EndIf
          (HttpVersion HttpStatus HttpMessage HttpHeaders)←4↑dat
          HttpStatus←toInt HttpStatus
     
          :If ~HttpStatus∊301 302 303 307 308 ⍝ not redirected?
              →∆END⊣(rc msg)←¯1('Unexpected server response: ',⍕(HttpStatus HttpMessage))
          :EndIf
     
          :If 0∊⍴loc←HttpHeaders GetHeader'location'
              →∆END⊣(rc msg)←¯1 'Redirection detected without "Location" header'
          :EndIf
     
          redirections+←1
          :If MaxRedirections<redirections
              →∆END⊣(rc msg)←¯1('Redirections exceeded maximum (',(⍕MaxRedirections),')')
          :EndIf
     
          Redirections,←t←⎕NS''
          t.(URL HttpVersion HttpStatus HttpMessage HttpHeaders)←(URL HttpVersion HttpStatus HttpMessage HttpHeaders)
          URL←loc
          {}LDRC.Close Connection
          →∆GET ⍝ try again
     
      :Case 'WSUpgrade'  ⍝ when WSAutoUpgrade is enabled
          →∆END⍴⍨0≠⊃(rc msg)←onWSUpgrade dat
          _listenerThread←Listen&obj
          Connected←1
          msg←'Connected'
          :If secure
          :AndIf 0=⊃z←LDRC.GetProp Connection'PeerCert'
              PeerCert←2⊃z
          :EndIf
          →∆EXIT
     
      :Case 'WSResponse' ⍝ when WSAutoUpgrade is not enabled (manual checking)
          :If 0=⊃(rc msg)←onWSResponse dat
              :If 0≠⊃err←LDRC.SetProp Connection'WSAccept'(dat'')
                  →∆END⊣(rc msg)←(⊃err)('Conga WSAccept failed: ',⍕err)
              :EndIf
          :Else
              →∆END⍴⍨0≠rc ⍝ exit if onWSReponse failed
          :EndIf
     
          _listenerThread←Listen&obj
          Connected←1
          msg←'Connected'
          :If secure
          :AndIf 0=⊃z←LDRC.GetProp Connection'PeerCert'
              PeerCert←2⊃z
          :EndIf
          →∆EXIT
     
      :Case 'Timeout'
          →∆END⊣(rc msg)←100 'Conga connection timed out'
     
      :Case 'Error'
          →∆END⊣(rc msg)←(4⊃ret)('Conga error processing your request: ',,⍕ret)
     
      :Case 'Closed'
          msg←'Socket closed by server'
          :If 0∊⍴HttpStatus
              rc←4⊃ret ⍝ set return code if closed before receiving HTTPHeader event
          :EndIf
          →∆END
     
      :Else
          →∆END⊣msg←'Unhandled Conga event type: ',evt ⍝ This shouldn't happen
      :EndSelect
     
     ∆END:
      Connection←{0::'' ⋄ ''⊣LDRC.Close ⍵}Connection
      ⎕TKILL _listenerThread
      _listenerThread←⍬
      Connected←0
     ∆EXIT:
    ∇

    ∇ Listen conx;rc;obj;evt;data;ret
      _done←0
      :While ~_done
          :Trap Debug↓0
              ret←LDRC.Wait conx WaitTime
              :If 'Timeout'≢3⊃ret ⋄ LastWaitResponse←ret ⋄ :EndIf
              :If 0≠⊃(rc obj evt data)←4↑ret
                  ⎕←'Conga Wait error: ',⍕ret
                  →∆END
              :EndIf
              :Select evt
              :Case 'WSReceive'
                  :If 0 2∊⍨⎕DR 0⍴1⊃data ⍝ character?
                      data[1]←⊂'UTF-8'⎕UCS ⎕UCS 1⊃data ⍝ WebSocket character data is UTF-8
                  :EndIf
                  onWSReceive data
              :Case 'Closed'
                  onClose ret
                  →∆END
              :Case 'Error'
                  onError ret
                  →∆END
              :Case 'Timeout' ⍝ do nothing
              :Else
                  ⎕←'Unhandled Conga event: ',⍕evt
                  →∆END
              :EndSelect
          :Else ⍝ :Trap
              ErrorInfo←⎕DMX ⍝ capture error information
              _done←1 ⍝ stop listening
          :EndTrap
      :EndWhile
      :Trap 0 ⋄ {}LDRC.Close conx ⋄ :EndTrap
     ∆END:
      (_done Connected)←1 0
    ∇

    NL←⎕UCS 13 10
    lc←¯3∘⎕C ⍝ lower case conversion
    uc←1∘⎕C  ⍝ upper case conversion
    ci←{⍺ ⍺⍺⍥lc ⍵} ⍝ case insensitive operator
    deb←' '∘(1↓,(/⍨)1(⊢∨⌽)0,≠) ⍝ delete extraneous blanks
    dlb←{(+/∧\' '=⍵)↓⍵} ⍝ delete leading blanks
    iotaz←((≢⊣)(≥×⊢)⍳)
    nameClass←{⍺←⎕THIS ⋄ ⍺.⎕NC⊂,'⍵'} ⍝ name class of argument
    splitOnN←{(≢⍺⍺)↓¨t⊆⍨(1+⍵⍵)⌊+\⍺⍺⍷t←⍺⍺,⍵} ⍝ (' ' splitOnN 2) 'this is a test' →→ 'this' 'is' 'a test'
    splitOnFirst←{(⍺↑⍨¯1+p)(⍺↓⍨p←⌊/⍺⍳⍵)} ⍝ split ⍺ on first occurrence of ⍵ (removing first ⍵)
    splitOn←(~∊)⊆⊣ ⍝ split ⍺ on all ⍵ (removing ⍵)
    toInt←{0∊⍴⍵:⍬ ⋄ ~3 5∊⍨10|⎕DR t←1⊃2⊃⎕VFI⍕⍵:⍬ ⋄ t≠⌊t:⍬ ⋄ t} ⍝ simple char to int
    getHeader←{⍺{1<|≡⍵:⍺∘∇¨⍵ ⋄ (⍺[;2],⊂'∘???∘')⊃⍨⍺[;1](⍳ci)⊆,⍵}⍵} ⍝ return header value(s) or '∘???∘' if not found
    beginsWith←{∧/⍵=⍺↑⍨≢⍵}
    isChar←{1≥|≡⍵:0 2∊⍨10|⎕DR{⊃⍣(0∊⍴⍵)⊢⍵}⍵ ⋄ ∧/∇¨⍵}
    isSimpleChar←{1≥|≡⍵:isChar ⍵ ⋄ 0}
    stopIf←{1∊⍵:-⎕TRAP←0 'C' '⎕←''Stopped for debugging... (Press Ctrl-Enter)''' ⋄ shy←0} ⍝ faster alternative to setting ⎕STOP
    atLeast←{a←(≢⍵)↑⍺ ⋄ ⊃((~∧\⍵=a)/a>⍵),1} ⍝ checks if ⍺ is at least version ⍵

    ∇ r←parseWSUpgrade dat;car;cdr;h;version;status;message;payload;headers
    ⍝ parses the data component of the WSUpgrade/WSResponse events (it's just a typical HTTP response)
      (car cdr)←(NL splitOnN 1)dat ⍝ split off the status line from the rest (yes, car and cdr are a LISP homage)
      (version status message)←(' 'splitOnN 2)car ⍝ split into HTTP version, HTTP status, HTTP message
      status←toInt status ⍝ status is a number
      (h payload)←((NL,NL)splitOnN 1)cdr ⍝ split headers from payload
      headers←dlb¨↑(':'splitOnN 1)¨h splitOn NL ⍝ split each header on first ':'
      r←⎕NS'version' 'status' 'message' 'headers' 'payload'
    ∇

    ∇ r←makeHeaders w
      r←{
          0::¯1            ⍝ any error
          ¯1∊⍵:⍵
          0∊⍴⍵:0 2⍴⊂''     ⍝ empty
          1≥|≡⍵:∇{         ⍝ simple array
              2=⍴⍵:1⊂⍵     ⍝ degenerate case of scalar name and value ('n' 'v' ≡ 'nv')
              dlb¨¨((,⍵)((~∊)⊆⊣)NL)splitOnFirst¨':'
          }⍵
          2=⍴⍴⍵:{          ⍝ matrix
              0∊≢¨⍵[;1]:¯1 ⍝ no empty names
              0 1 1/0,,¨⍵  ⍝ ensure it's 2 columns
          }⍵
          3=|≡⍵:∇{         ⍝ depth 3
              2|≢⊃,/⍵:¯1   ⍝ ensure an even number of element
              ↑⍵
          }(eis,)¨⍵
          2=|≡⍵:∇{
              ∧/':'∊¨⍵:⍵ splitOnFirst¨':'
              ((0.5×⍴⍵),2)⍴⍵
          }⍵
          ¯1
      }w
      'Invalid Headers format'⎕SIGNAL 7/⍨r≡¯1
    ∇

    ∇ r←GetEnv var
    ⍝ return enviroment variable setting for var
      :Access public shared
      r←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment'var
    ∇

    ∇ r←dyalogRoot
    ⍝ return path to interpreter
      r←{⍵,('/\'∊⍨⊢/⍵)↓'/'}{0∊⍴t←GetEnv'DYALOG':⊃1 ⎕NPARTS⊃2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetCommandLineArgs' ⋄ t}''
    ∇

    ∇ ns←ConnectionProperties url;p;defaultPort;ind;msg;protocol;secure;auth;host;port;path;urlparms
    ⍝ return namespace of connection properties based on parsing the supplied URL
      ns←⎕NS''
      msg←''
      (protocol secure host path urlparms)←parseURL url
     
      :If ~(⊂protocol)∊'' 'ws:' 'wss:' 'http:' 'https:'
          →∆END⊣msg←'Invalid protocol: ',¯1↓protocol
      :EndIf
     
      auth←''
      :If 0≠p←¯1↑⍸host='@' ⍝ Handle user:password@host...
          auth←('Basic ',(Base64Encode(p-1)↑host))
          host←p↓host
      :EndIf
     
    ⍝ This next section is a chicken and egg scenario trying to figure out
    ⍝ whether to use HTTPS as well as what port to use
     
      :If defaultPort←(≢host)<ind←host⍳':' ⍝ then if there's no port specified in the host
          port←(1+secure)⊃80 443 ⍝ use the default HTTP/HTTPS port
      :Else
          :If 0=port←⊃toInt ind↓host
              →∆END⊣msg←'Invalid host/port: ',host
          :EndIf
          host↑⍨←ind-1
      :EndIf
     
      :If 0∊⍴host
          →∆END⊣msg←'No host specified'
      :EndIf
     
      :If ~(port>0)∧(port≤65535)∧port=⌊port
          →∆END⊣msg←'Invalid port: ',⍕port
      :EndIf
     
      secure∨←(0∊⍴protocol)∧port=443 ⍝ if just port 443 was specified, without any protocol, use SSL
     
      :If defaultPort∧secure
          port←443
      :EndIf
     
      ns.(protocol secure auth host port path urlparms defaultPort)←protocol secure auth host port path urlparms defaultPort
     
     ∆END:
      ns.msg←msg
    ∇

    ∇ (protocol secure host path urlparms)←parseURL url;path;p;ind
    ⍝ Parses a URL and returns
    ⍝   protocol -  protocol (http, https, ws, wss)
    ⍝   secure - Boolean whether running HTTPS or not based on leading http://
    ⍝   host - domain or IP address
    ⍝   path - path on the host for the requested resource, if any
    ⍝   urlparms - URL query string, if any
      (url urlparms)←2↑(url splitOnFirst'?'),⊂''
      p←⍬⍴2+⍸<\'://'⍷url
      protocol←lc(0⌈p-2)↑url
      secure←∨/protocol∘beginsWith¨'wss:' 'https:'
      url←p↓url                          ⍝ Remove HTTP[s]:// if present
      (host path)←url splitOnFirst'/'    ⍝ Extract host and path from url
      ind←host iotaz'@'                  ⍝ any credentials?
      host←(ind↑host),lc ind↓host        ⍝ host (domain) is case-insensitive (credentials are not)
      path←'/',∊(⊂'%20')@(=∘' ')⊢path    ⍝ convert spaces in path name to %20
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←{name}AddHeader value;hdrs
    ⍝ add a header unless it's already defined
      :Access public
      :If 0=⎕NC'name' ⋄ (name value)←(⊃value)(1↓value) ⋄ :EndIf
      :Trap 7
          r←Headers←name(Headers addHeader)value
      :Else
          ⎕EM ⎕SIGNAL ⎕EN
      :EndTrap
    ∇

    ∇ value←{hdrs}GetHeader name
    ⍝ retrieve a header value
      :Access public
      hdrs←{6::⍵ ⋄ hdrs}Headers
      value←('∘???∘'∘≢⊢⍤/⊢)hdrs getHeader name
    ∇

    ∇ hdrs←name(hdrs addHeader)value
    ⍝ add a header unless it's already defined
      hdrs←makeHeaders hdrs
      :If ~0∊⍴value
          hdrs⍪←('∘???∘'≡hdrs getHeader name)⌿⍉⍪name value
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←{name}SetHeader value;ind
    ⍝ set a header value, overwriting any existing one
      :Access public
      :If 0=⎕NC'name' ⋄ (name value)←(⊃value)(1↓value) ⋄ :EndIf
      :Trap 7
          r←Headers←name(Headers setHeader)value
      :Else
          ⎕EM ⎕SIGNAL ⎕EN
      :EndTrap
    ∇

    ∇ hdrs←name(hdrs setHeader)value;ind
      hdrs←makeHeaders hdrs
      ind←hdrs[;1](⍳ci)eis name
      hdrs↑⍨←ind⌈≢hdrs
      hdrs[ind;]←name(⍕value)
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←RemoveHeader name
    ⍝ remove a header
      :Access public
      :Trap 7
          Headers←makeHeaders Headers
      :Else
          ⎕EM ⎕SIGNAL ⎕EN
      :EndTrap
      Headers⌿⍨←Headers[;1](≢¨ci)eis name
      r←Headers
    ∇

    ∇ r←formatHeaders hdrs
      r←2↓∊((⊂NL)':'),¨⍤1⊢hdrs
    ∇

    ∇ hdrs←environment hdrs;beg;end;escape;hits;regex
    ⍝ substitute any header names or values that begin with '$env:' with the named environment variable
      :If ~0∊⍴HeaderSubstitution
          (beg end)←2⍴HeaderSubstitution
          escape←'.^$*+?()[]{\|-'∘{m←∊(1+⍺∊⍨t←⌽⍵)↑¨1 ⋄ t←m\t ⋄ t[⍸~m]←'\' ⋄ ⌽t} ⍝ chars that need escaping in regex
          regex←(escape beg),'[[:alpha:]].*?',escape end
          hdrs←(⍴hdrs)⍴regex ⎕R{0∊⍴e←GetEnv(≢beg)↓(-≢end)↓⍵.Match:⍵.Match ⋄ e}⊢,hdrs
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ hdrs←privatize hdrs
    ⍝ suppress displaying Authorization header value if Private=1
      :If Secret
          hdrs[⍸hdrs[;1](∊ci)'Authorization' 'Proxy-Authorization';2]←⊂'>>> Secret setting is 1 <<<'
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←{a}eis w;f
    ⍝ enclose if simple
      f←{⍺←1 ⋄ ,(⊂⍣(⍺=|≡⍵))⍵}
      :If 0=⎕NC'a' ⋄ r←f w
      :Else ⋄ r←a f w
      :EndIf
    ∇

      base64←{(⎕IO ⎕ML)←0 1            ⍝ from dfns workspace - Base64 encoding and decoding as used in MIME.
          chars←'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/'
          bits←{,⍉(⍺⍴2)⊤⍵}             ⍝ encode each element of ⍵ in ⍺ bits, and catenate them all together
          part←{((⍴⍵)⍴⍺↑1)⊂⍵}          ⍝ partition ⍵ into chunks of length ⍺
          0=2|⎕DR ⍵:2∘⊥∘(8∘↑)¨8 part{(-8|⍴⍵)↓⍵}6 bits{(⍵≠64)/⍵}chars⍳⍵  ⍝ decode a string into octets
          four←{                       ⍝ use 4 characters to encode either
              8=⍴⍵:'=='∇ ⍵,0 0 0 0     ⍝   1,
              16=⍴⍵:'='∇ ⍵,0 0         ⍝   2
              chars[2∘⊥¨6 part ⍵],⍺    ⍝   or 3 octets of input
          }
          cats←⊃∘(,/)∘((⊂'')∘,)        ⍝ catenate zero or more strings
          cats''∘four¨24 part 8 bits ⍵
      }

    ∇ r←{cpo}Base64Encode w
    ⍝ Base64 Encode
    ⍝ Optional cpo (code points only) suppresses UTF-8 translation
    ⍝ if w is integer skip any conversion
      :Access public shared
      :If (⎕DR w)∊83 163 ⋄ r←base64 w
      :ElseIf 0=⎕NC'cpo' ⋄ r←base64'UTF-8'⎕UCS w
      :Else ⋄ r←base64 ⎕UCS w
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←{cpo}Base64Decode w
    ⍝ Base64 Decode
    ⍝ Optional cpo (code points only) suppresses UTF-8 translation
      :Access public shared
      :If 0=⎕NC'cpo' ⋄ r←'UTF-8'⎕UCS base64 w
      :Else ⋄ r←⎕UCS base64 w
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←{name}UrlEncode data;⎕IO;format;noname;xlate;hex
    ⍝ data is one of:
    ⍝      - a simple character vector (no name supplied)
    ⍝      - an even number of name/data character vectors
    ⍝       'name' 'fred' 'type' 'student' > 'name=fred&type=student'
    ⍝      - a namespace containing variable(s) to be encoded
    ⍝ r    is a character vector of the URLEncoded data
     
      :Access Public Shared
      ⎕IO←0
      format←{
          1=≡⍵:⍺(,⍕⍵)
          ↑⍺∘{⍺(,⍕⍵)}¨⍵
      }
      :If 0=⎕NC'name' ⋄ name←'' ⋄ :EndIf
      noname←0
      :If 9.1=⎕NC⊂'data'
          data←⊃⍪/{0∊⍴t←⍵.⎕NL ¯2:'' ⋄ ⍵{⍵ format ⍺⍎⍵}¨t}data
      :Else
          :Select |≡data
          :CaseList 0 1
              :If 1≥|≡data
                  noname←0∊⍴name
                  data←name(,data)
              :EndIf
          :Case 3 ⍝ nested name/value pairs (('abc' '123')('def' '789'))
              data←⊃,/data
          :EndSelect
      :EndIf
      hex←'%',¨,∘.,⍨⎕D,6↑⎕A
      xlate←{
          i←⍸~⍵∊'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789-_.~*'
          0∊⍴i:⍵
          ∊({⊂∊hex['UTF-8'⎕UCS ⍵]}¨⍵[i])@i⊢⍵
      }
      data←xlate∘⍕¨data
      r←noname↓¯1↓∊data,¨(⍴data)⍴'=&'
    ∇

:EndClass

